   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Whip Pan\n\nA fast directional cut: both scenes fly through the frame in one camera whip, with motion blur and a slight smear at peak speed. Plays between two placeholder panels.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 3.8 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Cuts need to feel fast and energetic: feature-to-feature jumps, montage rhythm, tech demos.\n- Scenes are peers in a sequence and the narrative moves sideways (or up and down a stack).\n- You need the workhorse directional cut.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The moment is calm or contemplative: use focus-pull.\n- More than about 3 whips in a row in the same direction: vary direction or alternate with fade-through.\n\nVariables:\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"left\"\n- blur (number, 0-48): Blur, default 24\n- scene_a_text (string): Scene A text, default \"Scene A\"\n- scene_b_text (string): Scene B text, default \"Scene B\"\n- scene_a_color (color): Scene A background, default \"#141318\"\n- scene_b_color (color): Scene B background, default \"#1a1922\"\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#f2f2f2\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Whip Pan\n\n  Whip the camera sideways with motion blur so both scenes fly through the frame in one move. remocn's version is a the source framework transition presentation; this block plays it between two placeholder panels (A and B). To use it in a video, put your own scenes in place of the panels and apply the same transform, blur and smear to both.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/whip-pan/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"whip-pan\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3.8\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"direction\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Direction\", \"description\": \"Direction the camera whips.\", \"default\": \"left\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"left\", \"label\": \"Left\"}, {\"value\": \"right\", \"label\": \"Right\"}, {\"value\": \"up\", \"label\": \"Up\"}, {\"value\": \"down\", \"label\": \"Down\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"blur\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Blur\", \"description\": \"Peak motion blur in pixels.\", \"default\": 24, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 48, \"step\": 2, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scene_a_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene A text\", \"description\": \"Label on the outgoing panel.\", \"default\": \"Scene A\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scene_b_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene B text\", \"description\": \"Label on the incoming panel.\", \"default\": \"Scene B\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scene_a_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Scene A background\", \"description\": \"Background of the outgoing panel.\", \"default\": \"#141318\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scene_b_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Scene B background\", \"description\": \"Background of the incoming panel.\", \"default\": \"#1a1922\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Panel text color.\", \"default\": \"#f2f2f2\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Whip Pan</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n          color: var(--color, #f2f2f2);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif);\n        }\n        .wp-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .wp-panel { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; will-change: transform, filter; }\n        .wp-label { font-size: 8.9cqmin; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; white-space: nowrap; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"whip-pan\" data-duration=\"3.8\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wp-clip\" class=\"wp-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3.8\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wp-a\" class=\"wp-panel\"><span id=\"wp-a-label\" class=\"wp-label\"></span></div>\n          <div id=\"wp-b\" class=\"wp-panel\"><span id=\"wp-b-label\" class=\"wp-label\"></span></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            // Easing.bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) as a function of t (Newton, then bisection).\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              function cx(s) { return 3 * x1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * x2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              function cy(s) { return 3 * y1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * y2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              return function (t) {\n                if (t <= 0) return 0;\n                if (t >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, s = t;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                  var x = cx(s);\n                  if (Math.abs(x - t) < 1e-6) break;\n                  if (x < t) lo = s; else hi = s;\n                  s = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return cy(s);\n              };\n            }\n            // interpolate(f, [a, b], [from, to]) with both ends clamped, like the source framework's extrapolate \"clamp\".\n            function interp(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var t = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(t) : t);\n            }\n            // Fit one line to 90 % of the frame width: shrinks the font size when it overflows.\n            function fit(root, line, size) {\n              line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * 0.9);\n              if (line.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / line.scrollWidth));\n                line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            // Drives draw(frame) from the paused timeline: frame = time * 30 * speed (the source framework's useCurrentFrame() * speed).\n            function drive(tl, total, speed, draw) {\n              var clock = { t: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { t: total, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t * 30 * speed); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3.8\");\n            var direction = pick(vars.direction, [\"left\", \"right\", \"up\", \"down\"], \"left\");\n            var blur = num(vars.blur, 24, 0, 48);\n            var a = document.getElementById(\"wp-a\");\n            var b = document.getElementById(\"wp-b\");\n            document.getElementById(\"wp-a-label\").textContent = str(vars.scene_a_text, \"Scene A\");\n            document.getElementById(\"wp-b-label\").textContent = str(vars.scene_b_text, \"Scene B\");\n            a.style.background = str(vars.scene_a_color, \"#141318\");\n            b.style.background = str(vars.scene_b_color, \"#1a1922\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n\n            // remocn timeline: scene A holds 70 frames, scene B 70, the transition is 26 frames and\n            // overlaps both, so it starts at frame 44 and the clip is 114 frames long.\n            var START = 44, LENGTH = 26;\n            var ease = bez(0.7, 0, 0.2, 1);\n            var axisX = direction === \"left\" || direction === \"right\";\n            var sign = direction === \"left\" || direction === \"up\" ? -1 : 1;\n            function place(el, entering, p) {\n              var travel = interp(p, 0, 1, 0, 1, ease);\n              var velocity = Math.sin(Math.PI * travel);\n              var offset = entering ? (travel - 1) * 110 * sign : travel * 110 * sign;\n              var stretch = 1 + velocity * 0.12;\n              el.style.transform = (axisX ? \"translate(\" + offset + \"%, 0)\" : \"translate(0, \" + offset + \"%)\") +\n                \" scale(\" + (axisX ? stretch + \", 1\" : \"1, \" + stretch) + \")\";\n              el.style.filter = velocity * blur > 0.01 ? \"blur(\" + velocity * blur + \"px)\" : \"none\";\n            }\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (frame - START) / LENGTH));\n              place(a, false, p);\n              place(b, true, p);\n              a.style.visibility = p >= 1 ? \"hidden\" : \"visible\";\n              b.style.visibility = p <= 0 ? \"hidden\" : \"visible\";\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            drive(tl, total, 1, draw);\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"whip-pan\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
